            "review_title": "Review at Thanh Nien",
            "review_text": "Jomax100\nPerth, Australia109 contributions\n0\nAuthentic\nDec 2017\nWe walked beyond Notre Dame Cathedral as far as Nguyen Van Chien St looking for a local restaurant. Thanh Nien had a range of set menus from which to choose, and a buffet was also on offer for 28 000VD. We settled on that and took a table in the air conditioned section in preference to eating outdoors.\nSeveral live cooking stations were set up - barbecue, noodle, etc - and soup, salads, seafood, curry and meat dishes were constantly replenished. Desserts of fresh fruit, sago pudding and cakes were offered, as were drinks (cordial?) and ice cream. We were uncertain what some of the dishes were, but it all seemed fresh and was tasty.\nThis was very much a local restaurant and many family groups were present on a Saturday evening. It is the sort of place you stumble across, or go with a local. We enjoyed the experience and considered it value for money. We struggled with language but the staff members were friendly and helpful. A genuine local experience not pitched at the tourist.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 28, 2018",
